    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d635-a1">

                <pb facs="0750" n="II" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pgII"/>

                <head>Earl Russell to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office, </hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-10-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 2, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 29th ultimo, enclosing copies of communications which have
                    been made to you by the consul of the United States at Cape Town, relative to
                    the proceedings at that place of the steam vessel Alabama, and I beg to inform
                    you that the matter has already been brought to the notice of her Majesty’s
                    government, and is now under consideration.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
